  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening SDG Localization Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite the success of SDG-L 1.0 implementation and on-going effective interventions under SDG-L 1.5, several gaps (e.g. income disparity, climate challenges, gender inequality) remain. The proposed project Strengthening Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) Localization in Thailand &#x2013; Phase II (SDG-L 2.0) aims to advance the effective implementation of SDGs in Thailand, with particular emphasis on human rights, gender equality, environmental sustainability, and climate change adaptation and resilience, including at the subnational level. This initiative will further consolidate the EU-UN-Thailand partnership in the pursuit of Agenda 2030, creating platforms for dialogue among the EU, public authorities, civil society organizations (CSOs), academia, private sector, and other stakeholders across various levels.</narrative>
  </description>
